{"evt":"note_created","id":"note-mqb1ic5y3qr","workspace":"/Users/imyu/Desktop/zonoid","title":"Neural gate build sequence: labeler is critical path, shadow before enforce","summary":"Build sequencing (2026-06-12) for the learned context gate. Phases: (0 DONE) journal schema complete incl task-side features qWords/taskWords/hasSpec/complexity. (1) design + decisions in graph. (2 CRITICAL PATH) scripts/gate-label.js outcome-linkage labeler + FN post-mortem matcher in nightly QA — without it all journal data is unlabeled. (3) epsilon-exploration in gateTask: occasionally inject when the gate would abstain, to harvest abstain-region counterfactual outcomes — MUST land WITH the labeler (phase 2+3 parallel) so the unobserved-abstain selection bias is mitigated from day 1. (4) accumulate ~200-300 labeled rows, ~2-4 weeks of real traffic; the data clock effectively started today (pre-today rows lack task-side fields). (5) scripts/gate-train.js: LR + Platt calibration, train/val split BY TASK and TIME-ORDERED, eval REGRET vs the rule floor on the held-out 9-case ground truth (test/context-gate-regression.test.js) + bench arms — these are eval-only, NEVER training data (oracle-contamination lesson). (6) shadow-deploy the learned gate advisory (log its decision beside the rule's, don't enforce) until labeled comparison shows it wins. (7) enforce + ship the orchestrator-trained LR as global prior to user repos, Platt-recalibrate on first ~20-30 local outcomes. Acceptance bar to ship: learned regret <= rule-floor regret AND calibration within +/-0.1 on the reliability curve. Extends [[note-mqatnwimnk0]].","created_by":"main","valid_from":"2026-06-12T14:46:53.974Z","vec":[-0.11195631325244904,-0.0360984280705452,-0.05111357197165489,0.010570700280368328,-0.0027633395511657,0.03978800028562546,-0.0071027991361916065,-0.0015959114534780383,0.05704236403107643,-0.04995780810713768,0.05272803455591202,-0.06307237595319748,-0.08022959530353546,-0.02154192328453064,-0.0399704128503799